My recent study of the Edda taught me that Valkyries were also 
considered as the Fate--Goddesses of war in the sense that they 
were assigned by Odin with the task of killing particular persons 
in the battle, thus granting victory to the other side.  Bruenhilde 
was punished by Odin for having killed the leader Odin wanted to 
be victorious.  (A deep slumber, from which Sigurd awoke her finally; 
a surprisingly light-handed punishment in the world of murder and 
brutality the Edda depicts.)  

